class:: FreqToVolt
summary:: MS-20-inspired frequency-to-voltage event analysis
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIRa-MS20-ESP

description::
Four outputs: cv, frequency, eventRate, valid. All finite in [0,1]. Frequency indication is calibrated event evidence, not unique F0. Multiply unclipped frequency by referenceMaxFreq for indicated Hz.

All parameters except the signal input are construction-time numbers. Outputs are control rate. See the guide for calibration, clipping, latency and model limitations.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: in
Audio input; processed at audio sample granularity.

argument:: lowCut
Low cutoff in Hz; circuit mode couples this to output smoothing.

argument:: highCut
High cutoff in Hz; circuit mode uses two active low-pass sections.

argument:: cvAdjust
Fixed software calibration multiplier.

argument:: mode
Literal \digital or \circuit.

argument:: inputGain
Fixed gain; circuit frontend treats one amplified audio unit as one model volt.

argument:: threshold
Crossing threshold in conditioned input units.

argument:: hysteresis
Schmitt half-width; circuit mode enforces its assumed minimum.

argument:: pulseWidth
Circuit pulse duration in seconds; ignored in digital mode.

argument:: smoothTime
Digital averaging time in seconds; ignored in circuit mode.

argument:: referenceMaxFreq
Fixed frequency reference, default 2000 Hz. Also determines software voltage calibration.

argument:: referenceMaxEventRate
Fixed event-rate reference, default 4000 events per second.

argument:: timeout
Evidence timeout in seconds.

returns::
Four outputs: cv, frequency, eventRate, valid. All finite in [0,1]. Frequency indication is calibrated event evidence, not unique F0. Multiply unclipped frequency by referenceMaxFreq for indicated Hz.

examples::
Loop SuperCollider's bundled voice recording and use the extracted pitch to drive an LFSaw. The three choices use vanilla Pitch, MIR2 PitchMPM, and FreqToVolt. FreqToVolt counts conditioned events, so its indication can differ from the pitch estimators on speech.

First boot the server and load the recording. Run the next block after the buffer has loaded.
code::
s.waitForBoot {
    b = Buffer.read(s, Platform.resourceDir +/+ "sounds/a11wlk01.wav");
};
::

The same source feeds all three analyzers. Change which while listening. FreqToVolt's normalized frequency outlet is multiplied by its default 2000 Hz reference; the other two already return Hz. Source amplitude controls loudness.
code::
(
~pitchCompare = { |which = 0|
    var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, b, BufRateScale.kr(b), loop: 1);
    var vanilla = Pitch.kr(source)[0];
    var mir = PitchMPM.kr(source)[0];
    var fv = FreqToVolt.kr(source, mode: \digital)[1] * 2000;
    var hz = Select.kr(which, [vanilla, mir, fv]);
    var amp = Amplitude.kr(source);
    (LFSaw.ar(hz.clip(40, 2000)) * amp * 0.3) ! 2
}.play;
)
::

Select one extractor at a time:
code::
~pitchCompare.set(\which, 0); // vanilla Pitch
::
code::
~pitchCompare.set(\which, 1); // MIR2 PitchMPM
::
code::
~pitchCompare.set(\which, 2); // FreqToVolt
::

Stop and free the buffer when finished:
code::
~pitchCompare.free;
b.free;
::
